
Medical Triage Classification

Introduction:
This project aims to identify how serious a patient's health problem is by analyzing the symptoms they describe. 
It helps classify patient queries into different urgency levels so that healthcare professionals can understand which 
patients need immediate attention. Based on the symptoms, the system provides one of four categories: EMERGENCY, URGENT, ROUTINE, or INSUFFICIENT_DATA.

Prompt:
Read the patient's query carefully and identify the seriousness of the symptoms.
Classify the query into EMERGENCY, URGENT, ROUTINE, or INSUFFICIENT_DATA based on the given triage rules. 
If the symptoms indicate a life-threatening condition, choose EMERGENCY. If the patient needs medical attention soon, choose URGENT. 
For mild symptoms or general health questions, choose ROUTINE. If there is not enough information to identify the urgency, choose INSUFFICIENT_DATA. 
Never assume symptoms that the patient has not mentioned. If emergency symptoms are reported, prioritize emergency care. Return only one category without any explanation or additional text.

Sample Inputs and Expected Outputs

I suddenly feel very weak on one side of my body and cannot speak clearly.
EMERGENCY

I have been experiencing a fever along with a sore throat for two days.
URGENT

I have a slight cough, but I can do my daily activities normally. 
ROUTINE

I suddenly developed severe breathing difficulty while walking.
EMERGENCY

I have been feeling nauseous and have vomited several times today.
URGENT

I want to know how often I should have a general health checkup.
ROUTINE

I have a small skin rash that does not cause any pain.
ROUTINE

I am experiencing sudden severe abdominal pain.
EMERGENCY

I have been feeling sick for some time.
INSUFFICIENT_DATA

I have a mild headache and feel slightly tired today.
